Publication and recovery boundary
----------------------------------

The entry first checks its complete inputs, forecasts all output/read/path
costs and closes every input with a whole-file reread.  It then creates
only the new immutable epoch/stage outputs, writes their whole bodies
exclusively, flushes them, and verifies every output with closed reads.
A durable publication_intent.json records before/after pointers, exact
counts, changes, Source and Root decision before any active pointer moves.

A collective whole-file CAS checks all old active pointers, old runtime,
bank and receipt.  An immediate closed CAS checks each old pointer again
before its replacement.  Publication replaces L026 CURRENT, the controller
pointer and the intake pointer serially, with directory synchronization.
A complete post-publication read closes the new pointer/runtime/bank/
receipt joins.  The readback remains explicitly pending independent audit.

This is a serialized sole-writer protocol, not a locked atomic update of
three files.  Root must not admit another writer or start a new cohort
while publication is in progress.  A process or machine failure between
replacements can leave a partial pointer set.  The durable intent and exact
before/after images make that state reviewable.  Do not rerun this entry
or replay science to repair it: the fresh epoch and typed-status checks
will reject a second registration.  Root must use a separately reviewed
metadata repair/roll-forward from the retained images if required.

